  "worked_solution": "First, remember that a fraction represents a division.  So, a fraction of fractions is a division of two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,(-\\frac{5}{4})\\,}{(-\\frac{1}{8})}=(-\\frac{5}{4})÷(-\\frac{1}{8})\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $-\\frac{1}{8}$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $-\\frac{8}{1}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{5}{4})÷(-\\frac{1}{8}) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{5}{4})\\times (-\\frac{8}{1}) & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\times 8}{4\\times 1} & = \\\\ \\frac{40}{4} & = \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\,(-\\frac{5}{4})\\,}{(-\\frac{1}{8})}=10.\n$$",
